title: Your Inner Circle
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
card-image: img/party.svg
view-if: inner_circle_timer <= 0 and difficulty >= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inner_circle_timer = 8
go-to: rm_main

Changing the people closest to you is painful, but perhaps it is necessary.

Dropping an adviser angers their faction of the party; bringing one in strengthens their faction. You can have three at a time.

@rm_main
title: Drop advisers.

- #remove_advisor
- @add_advisors: Bring in advisers.

@add_advisors
title: Bring in advisers.
choose-if: n_advisors < 3
unavailable-subtitle: A maximum of three advisers.

- #add_advisor
- @rm_main: Drop advisers instead.
- @remove_none: Stop changing advisers.

@remove_none
title: Stop changing advisers.
go-to: root
tags: remove_advisor

#################### dropping

@remove_whitelaw
title: Drop Willie Whitelaw
view-if: whitelaw_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: whitelaw_advisor = 0; loyalist_dissent += 8; n_advisors -= 1
go-to: rm_main

Whitelaw takes it with good grace in public. The party managers are shaken.

@remove_joseph
title: Drop Sir Keith Joseph
view-if: joseph_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: joseph_advisor = 0; dry_dissent += 5; n_advisors -= 1
go-to: rm_main

The dries wonder whether you still believe what they believe.

@remove_howe
title: Drop Sir Geoffrey Howe
view-if: howe_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: howe_advisor = 0; dry_dissent += 5; n_advisors -= 1
go-to: rm_main

Howe accepts it without complaint, as he accepts most things. The dries notice.

@remove_reece
title: Drop Gordon Reece
view-if: reece_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: reece_advisor = 0; n_advisors -= 1
go-to: rm_main

Reece goes back to the private sector, and to his cigars.

@remove_prior
title: Drop Jim Prior
view-if: prior_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: prior_advisor = 0; wet_dissent += 5; n_advisors -= 1
go-to: rm_main

The wets take it as a declaration of war.

@remove_pym
title: Drop Francis Pym
view-if: pym_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: pym_advisor = 0; wet_dissent += 5; n_advisors -= 1
go-to: rm_main

Pym says nothing in public and a great deal in private.

@remove_heseltine
title: Drop Michael Heseltine
view-if: heseltine_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: heseltine_advisor = 0; wet_dissent += 5; n_advisors -= 1
go-to: rm_main

Heseltine goes off to build his own following.

@remove_carrington
title: Drop Lord Carrington
view-if: carrington_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: carrington_advisor = 0; loyalist_dissent += 5; n_advisors -= 1
go-to: rm_main

The grandees are puzzled.

@remove_tebbit
title: Drop Norman Tebbit
view-if: tebbit_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: tebbit_advisor = 0; right_dissent += 5; n_advisors -= 1
go-to: rm_main

The right feels it has lost its voice in Number 10.

@remove_lawson
title: Drop Nigel Lawson
view-if: lawson_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: lawson_advisor = 0; dry_dissent += 4; n_advisors -= 1
go-to: rm_main

Lawson goes back to his department, convinced that he could do your job better than you.

@remove_gilmour
title: Drop Sir Ian Gilmour
view-if: gilmour_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: {!
Q.gilmour_advisor = 0;
Q.wet_dissent += 6;
Q.n_advisors -= 1;
if (Q.con_in_government) {
    this.achieve('full_speed_ahead');
}
!}
go-to: rm_main

[? if con_in_government = 1 : Gilmour leaves Downing Street and tells the waiting cameras: "It does no harm to throw the occasional man overboard, but it does not do much good if you are steering full speed ahead for the rocks." ?][? if con_in_government = 0 : Gilmour takes it with aristocratic indifference. The wets take it less well. ?]

@remove_parkinson
title: Drop Cecil Parkinson
view-if: parkinson_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: parkinson_advisor = 0; loyalist_dissent += 4; n_advisors -= 1
go-to: rm_main

Parkinson takes it with a smile. Central Office is less cheerful.

@remove_biffen
title: Drop John Biffen
view-if: biffen_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: biffen_advisor = 0; dry_dissent += 3; wet_dissent += 2; n_advisors -= 1
go-to: rm_main

Biffen retreats to his farm in Shropshire and his weekly column, wryly.

@remove_brittan
title: Drop Leon Brittan
view-if: brittan_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: brittan_advisor = 0; dry_dissent += 3; n_advisors -= 1
go-to: rm_main

Brittan returns to his brief without complaint.

@remove_nott
title: Drop John Nott
view-if: nott_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: nott_advisor = 0; dry_dissent += 3; n_advisors -= 1
go-to: rm_main

Nott mentions, not for the first time, that he'd rather be in the City.

@remove_stevas
title: Drop Norman St John-Stevas
view-if: stevas_advisor = 1
tags: remove_advisor
on-arrival: stevas_advisor = 0; wet_dissent += 5; n_advisors -= 1
go-to: rm_main

St John-Stevas is the first of the wets to go, and he goes with a quip about the Blessed Margaret that is all over Westminster by teatime.

#################### bringing in

@add_whitelaw
title: Willie Whitelaw
subtitle: Loyalist. The party's great conciliator. {!<br><br>!}Actions: calm the wets, party discipline.
is-card: true
card-image: img/advisor_loyalist.svg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: whitelaw_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3
on-arrival: whitelaw_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1; loyalist_strength += 5; loyalist_dissent -= 3
go-to: add_advisors

@add_joseph
title: Sir Keith Joseph
subtitle: Dry. The intellectual engine of the new Conservatism. {!<br><br>!}Actions: lecture tour, Stepping Stones, back management.
is-card: true
card-image: img/advisor_dry.svg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: joseph_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3
on-arrival: joseph_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1; dry_strength += 5; dry_dissent -= 3
go-to: add_advisors

@add_howe
title: Sir Geoffrey Howe
subtitle: Dry. Relentless on economic detail. {!<br><br>!}Actions: alternative budget or emergency package, reassure the City.
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/howe.jpg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: howe_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3
on-arrival: howe_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1; dry_strength += 5; dry_dissent -= 3
go-to: add_advisors

@add_reece
title: Gordon Reece
subtitle: No faction. A television producer turned image-maker. {!<br><br>!}Actions: the makeover, the popular press.
is-card: true
card-image: img/advisor_none.svg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: reece_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3
on-arrival: reece_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1
go-to: add_advisors

@add_prior
title: Jim Prior
subtitle: Wet. A farmer with friends in the unions. {!<br><br>!}Actions: talk to the moderates, step-by-step union reform.
is-card: true
card-image: img/advisor_wet.svg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: prior_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3
on-arrival: prior_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1; wet_strength += 5; wet_dissent -= 5
go-to: add_advisors

@add_pym
title: Francis Pym
subtitle: Wet. A patrician pessimist and a safe pair of hands. {!<br><br>!}Actions: reassure the shires, foreign affairs.
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/pym.jpg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: pym_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3
on-arrival: pym_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1; wet_strength += 5; wet_dissent -= 5
go-to: add_advisors

@add_heseltine
title: Michael Heseltine
subtitle: Wet. Ambitious, flamboyant, the darling of the conference. {!<br><br>!}Actions: a conference speech, urban regeneration.
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/heseltine.jpg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: heseltine_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3
on-arrival: heseltine_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1; wet_strength += 5; wet_dissent -= 5
go-to: add_advisors

@add_carrington
title: Lord Carrington
subtitle: Loyalist. The grandest of the grandees. {!<br><br>!}Actions: diplomacy, steady the Lords.
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/carrington.jpg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: carrington_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3 and foreign_secretary == "Carrington"
on-arrival: carrington_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1; loyalist_strength += 5; loyalist_dissent -= 3
go-to: add_advisors

@add_tebbit
title: Norman Tebbit
subtitle: Right. A street fighter who enjoys the fight. {!<br><br>!}Actions: savage Labour or a new Employment Act, "On your bike".
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/tebbit.jpg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: tebbit_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3
on-arrival: tebbit_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1; right_strength += 5; right_dissent -= 5
go-to: add_advisors

@add_lawson
title: Nigel Lawson
subtitle: Dry. A combative former financial journalist. {!<br><br>!}Actions: a tax reform plan or the Medium-Term Financial Strategy, prepare for the miners, brief the City.
is-card: true
card-image: img/advisor_dry.svg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: lawson_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3
on-arrival: lawson_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1; dry_strength += 5; dry_dissent -= 3
go-to: add_advisors

@add_gilmour
title: Sir Ian Gilmour
subtitle: Wet. The most articulate critic of monetarism. {!<br><br>!}Actions: One Nation, the armed forces or Europe, temper the monetarists.
is-card: true
card-image: img/advisor_wet.svg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: gilmour_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3
on-arrival: gilmour_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1; wet_strength += 5; wet_dissent -= 5
go-to: add_advisors

@add_parkinson
title: Cecil Parkinson
subtitle: Loyalist. A smooth organiser and fundraiser. {!<br><br>!}Actions: business dinners, small business, plan the campaign, run the party machine.
is-card: true
card-image: img/advisor_loyalist.svg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: parkinson_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3
on-arrival: parkinson_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1; loyalist_strength += 5; loyalist_dissent -= 3
go-to: add_advisors

@add_biffen
title: John Biffen
subtitle: Dry, but a consolidator. {!<br><br>!}Actions: the free-market case, cash limits, manage the Commons, counsel consolidation.
is-card: true
card-image: img/advisor_dry.svg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: biffen_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3
on-arrival: biffen_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1; dry_strength += 4; dry_dissent -= 2; wet_dissent -= 2
go-to: add_advisors

@add_brittan
title: Leon Brittan
subtitle: Dry. A barrister with a formidable grasp of detail. {!<br><br>!}Actions: attack the Scotland Bill, Question Time briefings, a spending review, the police bill.
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/brittan.jpg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: brittan_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3
on-arrival: brittan_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1; dry_strength += 5; dry_dissent -= 3
go-to: add_advisors

@add_nott
title: John Nott
subtitle: Dry. A merchant banker with no sentiment about the Navy. {!<br><br>!}Actions: free trade, the Price Commission, the defence review, the task force.
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/nott.jpg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: nott_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3
on-arrival: nott_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1; dry_strength += 5; dry_dissent -= 3
go-to: add_advisors

@add_stevas
title: Norman St John-Stevas
subtitle: Wet. Witty, theatrical, and a parliamentarian to his fingertips. {!<br><br>!}Actions: parents' rights, charm the House, select committees, the arts.
is-card: true
card-image: img/advisor_wet.svg
tags: add_advisor
view-if: stevas_advisor = 0 and n_advisors < 3
on-arrival: stevas_advisor = 1; n_advisors += 1; wet_strength += 5; wet_dissent -= 5
go-to: add_advisors
